1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:04,353
A coffee cup lands on the counter. Its
price is eight dollars.

2
00:00:04,353 --> 00:00:07,439
Two bright offers appear, and each
promises a better deal.

3
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:19,109
The first offer removes twenty-five
percent of the price.

4
00:00:19,109 --> 00:00:24,106
A quarter of the paper price tag folds
away, leaving a smaller amount.

5
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,404
The second offer removes one dollar and
fifty cents.

6
00:00:33,404 --> 00:00:37,383
This saving stays the same even when the
original coffee price begins to

7
00:00:37,383 --> 00:00:37,689
change.

8
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:51,230
Two receipts grow beside the cup. Their
lengths represent the money you pay.

9
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:55,522
Which receipt should be shorter at an
eight-dollar menu price?

10
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:04,220
Now imagine another café with a different
menu price.

11
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:06,996
A percentage saving changes with that
price.

12
00:01:06,996 --> 00:01:09,772
A fixed saving does not follow it.

13
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:20,995
Pause at the counter before you buy. Name
the base price, calculate both

14
00:01:20,995 --> 00:01:25,106
payments, and explain which offer gives
you the better deal.
